---
import ServicePage from '../layouts/ServicePage.astro';
import { eastAuckland } from '../data/qa';
import photo from '../assets/photos/ropes.jpg';
---

<ServicePage
  place
  title="Boat Cleaning East Auckland | Maraetai | Shore Leave"
  description="Boat cleaning in East Auckland. Trailer boat wash at home in Maraetai and Beachlands, plus berth resets at Pine Harbour. Provisioning too."
  crumb="Boat cleaning East Auckland"
  h1="East Auckland boats, reset where they sit."
  lede="Pine Harbour round to Maraetai. Further west? Ask, and we’ll be straight with you."
  photo={photo}
  photoAlt="Heavy rope coiled around a pair of bollards on a boat’s deck"
  faqs={eastAuckland}
  serviceName="Boat cleaning in East Auckland"
  og="east-auckland"
>
  <section class="wrap band">
    <div class="inset flow">
      <h2>The ramps we know, and how we cover them</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10 grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
      <div class="card flow">
        <h3>Maraetai</h3>
        <p>A concrete ramp at Maraetai Park and a timber ramp off Omana Esplanade. Tow home and let us know.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card flow">
        <h3>Beachlands</h3>
        <p>Sunkist Bay Reserve for trailer boats, Pine Harbour Marina for berths. This is where we spend most of our time.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card flow">
        <h3>Half Moon Bay, Howick and Bucklands Beach</h3>
        <p>These sit outside our regular run, so send your address and we’ll tell you honestly if we can do it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="bg-beige-2">
    <div class="wrap band">
      <div class="inset flow">
        <h2>Trailer boat wash, East Auckland style</h2>
        <p>Most East Auckland trailer boats do short, hard days: out to Waiheke, Rakino or the Firth, and back the same night. A reset the next day keeps the boat ready for the next good forecast.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServicePage>
